Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:18:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CI CRAFT 9.1: cinematic light rig, tier-aware shadows and
 fog, asphalt wear

Visual polish only. No world geometry, coordinates, collision, physics, hit
detection, networking or game rules are touched, and the map pipeline is
unchanged. Geometry audit confirms identical output: 712 meshes / 361,788
triangles, same as before.

Lighting (src/world/VisualAtmosphere.ts, src/core/GameEngine.ts)
- Day sun dropped from ~48 to ~35 degrees elevation and moved off-axis, so
  shadows are longer and buildings and trees get real directional form. The
  light rig moves; no world coordinate does.
- Ambient/key rebalanced: hemisphere 0.96 -> 0.66, sun 1.54 -> 1.86. Ambient
  near 0.96 lit shadowed faces almost as brightly as lit ones, which made the
  world read flat. Total light delivered is roughly unchanged, so nothing
  darkens overall.
- Day key light warmed 0xfffbeb -> 0xfff0d2 so sunlit stone and asphalt read
  warm against the cool sky.

Shadows, per quality tier (new getShadowRigForQuality)
- Was a fixed 1536 px map for every device. Now 1024 / 1536 / 2048 / 2048 with
  matching PCF radius and normal bias, so phones pay less and desktops get
  crisper contact shadows. Changing tier at runtime disposes and rebuilds the
  shadow target explicitly rather than silently doing nothing.

Fog, per quality tier (new getFogDensityForQuality)
- Distance fog scaled by tier: mobile a little denser, desktop clearer, so
  distant buildings stay readable. Applied to all three time-of-day presets.

Asphalt (src/world/RoadNetwork.ts)
- Two-scale deterministic wear instead of a single high-frequency jitter: a
  slow ~9 m resurfaced-patch layer under the existing fine grain, plus a
  slightly less uniform roughness (0.93 -> 0.90). Vertex colours only: no extra
  draw call, no texture, no geometry change, identical on every client.

Verification
- npm test 205/205, tsc clean, build 593 ms, geometry audit PASS.
- The new helpers were checked numerically (shadow rig and fog per tier, sun
  elevation 47.9 -> 34.9 deg).
- LIMITATION: the offline preview renderer shades with a hardcoded light term
  (light = 0.30 + skyUp*0.34 + lambert*0.85) and never reads hemiLight or
  dirLight, so it cannot show any of the lighting changes. Lighting is
  therefore NOT visually verified. No WebGL is available in this environment.

